[34m[38;5;88m    [34m[38;5;28m 52 [34m[32m#### Tmux 24bit color configuration[0m
[34m[38;5;88m    [34m[38;5;28m 53 [34m[32m If you're using tmux, it's worth checking that 24 bit color is  working correctly. For example, run a color test script like [this  one](https://gist.githubusercontent.com/lifepillar/09a44b8cf0f9397465614e622979107f/raw/24-bit-color.sh),  or the others listed at https://gist.github.com/XVilka/8346728. If  you do not see smooth color gradients, see the discussion at  [tmux#696](https://github.com/tmux/tmux/issues/696). The short  version is you need something like this in your `~/.tmux.conf`:[0m
[34m[38;5;88m    [34m[38;5;28m 54 [34m[32m ```[0m
[34m[38;5;88m    [34m[38;5;28m 55 [34m[32m set -ga terminal-overrides ",xterm-256color:Tc"[0m
[34m[38;5;88m    [34m[38;5;28m 56 [34m[32m ```[0m
[34m[38;5;88m    [34m[38;5;28m 57 [34m[32m and you may then  need to quit tmux completely for it to take effect.[0m
